		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Friction in Cline's paper: how to use?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=4436#p4436"><![CDATA[
The method Cline described is either Stewart-Trinkle or Anitescu-Potra. The resulting matrix cannot be solved by naive Lemke but can be solved quite efficiently using a specialized Lemke solver.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=225">ngbinh</a> — Wed Jun 06, 2007 5:41 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
